{
  "$comment": [
    "THE SCRIPT-AUTHORING EVAL CORPUS.",
    "",
    "WHAT IT IS: the tasks a model must handle for Calcula's AI to be useful, each",
    "with a REFERENCE solution that really works. Owner decision 2026-08-19 (design",
    "doc §11.3): this ships in-repo as a developer/CI artifact -- public, no UI, no",
    "support promise -- because withholding it would make every compatibility claim",
    "unfalsifiable, which is a poor look for a project whose pitch is auditability.",
    "",
    "TWO LAYERS, AND THE FIRST NEEDS NO MODEL AT ALL:",
    "  A. Every `reference` is validated by the real M2 validator in CI. A corpus",
    "     whose reference solutions do not pass is measuring nothing -- it would",
    "     score models against an API that does not exist. This is the layer that",
    "     keeps the corpus honest as the surface changes underneath it.",
    "  B. `tests/eval/run-eval.mjs` runs the intents through a real provider and",
    "     scores the output. That is what gives M7's `canaryScore` its meaning.",
    "",
    "`canary: true` marks the in-app probe subset. Both layers read THIS file, so",
    "the number a user sees in the model picker and the number CI reports cannot",
    "diverge.",
    "",
    "ADDING A TASK: write the reference FIRST and run `npm test`. If it fails L1 you",
    "invented a method; if it fails L2 your pragmas are wrong. Either way the task",
    "was not yet a fair test of anything.",
    "",
    "`outcome` (optional) is the EXPECTED-DIFF GRADE: seed `fixture` cells, fire the",
    "`event` handler, then require `expect` cells to hold these INPUT STRINGS (the",
    "same vocabulary ai_dry_run_script's readBack reports: formulas as '=...',",
    "integers without '.0', empty as \"\") and `expectOutput` substrings to appear in",
    "the script's log/notify output. `match` is a case-insensitive regex for cells",
    "with several equally-correct spellings; `matchOutput` is the same for output",
    "(anchor counts: a bare '3' substring also matches '13' and coordinates).",
    "`eventCount` fires the hook N times (a counter needs two clicks to differ from",
    "a reset); `stubs.failWrite` injects one write failure (an error-handling task",
    "needs an error). Everything an expectation pins must be NAMED IN THE INTENT.",
    "Layer A requires every reference to grade 1.0, which is what keeps the",
    "harness's semantics honest: if a reference grades below 1.0 the harness or",
    "the expectation is wrong, never the model."
  ],
  "version": 2,
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "grid-read-write-cell",
      "canary": true,
      "objectType": "button",
      "intent": "When this button is clicked, copy the value in A1 into B1.",
      "hints": ["cell", "copy", "value"],
      "expectCapabilities": [],
      "mustCall": ["onClick", "api.getCellValue", "api.setCellValue"],
      "reference": [
        "export function setup(context) {",
        "  context.onClick(async () => {",
        "    const value = await context.api.getCellValue(0, 0);",
        "    await context.api.setCellValue(0, 1, value);",
        "  });",
        "}"
      ],
      "outcome": {
        "event": "onClick",
        "fixture": [
          { "row": 0, "col": 0, "value": "42" }
        ],
        "expect": [
          { "row": 0, "col": 0, "value": "42" },
          { "row": 0, "col": 1, "value": "42" }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grid-sum-column",
      "canary": true,
      "objectType": "button",
      "intent": "Put a SUM formula in B101 that totals column B rows 2 to 100.",
      "hints": ["sum", "column", "total", "formula"],
      "expectCapabilities": [],
      "mustCall": ["onClick", "api.setCellFormula|api.setCellValue"],
      "reference": [
        "export function setup(context) {",
        "  context.onClick(async () => {",
        "    await context.api.setCellFormula(100, 1, '=SUM(B2:B100)');",
        "  });",
        "}"
      ],
      "outcome": {
        "event": "onClick",
        "fixture": [
          { "row": 1, "col": 1, "value": "10" },
          { "row": 2, "col": 1, "value": "20" },
          { "row": 3, "col": 1, "value": "30" }
        ],
        "expect": [
          { "row": 100, "col": 1, "match": "^=SUM\\(\\$?B\\$?2:\\$?B\\$?100\\)$" }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grid-sum-in-script",
      "canary": false,
      "objectType": "button",
      "intent": "Add up column B from row 2 to row 100 in the script itself (not with a formula) and write the number into B101.",
      "hints": ["sum", "add up", "range"],
      "expectCapabilities": [],
      "mustCall": ["onClick", "api.getRangeValues", "api.setCellValue"],
      "reference": [
        "export function setup(context) {",
        "  context.onClick(async () => {",
        "    const cells = await context.api.getRangeValues(1, 1, 99, 1);",
        "    let total = 0;",
        "    for (const row of cells) {",
        "      for (const cell of row) {",
        "        const n = Number(cell.value);",
        "        if (!Number.isNaN(n)) total += n;",
        "      }",
        "    }",
        "    await context.api.setCellValue(100, 1, total);",
        "  });",
        "}"
      ],
      "outcome": {
        "event": "onClick",
        "fixture": [
          { "row": 1, "col": 1, "value": "10" },
          { "row": 2, "col": 1, "value": "20" },
          { "row": 3, "col": 1, "value": "n/a" },
          { "row": 4, "col": 1, "value": "5.5" },
          { "row": 5, "col": 1, "value": "0.5" }
        ],
        "expect": [
          { "row": 100, "col": 1, "value": "36" }
        ]
      }
    },
